reply.body:
@NickleHuang @chrisvest Guys, have you tested the change, is there a unit test that covers this? 

If my reading of the code is correct there is no way to use new API from inside the `#getUnadjustedFrameLength(...)`. Say one calls `#resetFrameLengthInt()` inside `#getUnadjustedFrameLength(...)`, meaning it returns some frame length and also resets the `this.frameLengthInt` using provided API.

Look at [LengthFieldBasedFrameDecoder.java#L430](https://github.com/netty/netty/blob/14e33dbc2ed85c9965ee6dc3418f69d20bd13546/codec/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/LengthFieldBasedFrameDecoder.java#L430), it looks like the `this.frameLengthInt` is overwritten with the frame length. I think this needs fixing.
